 36S  c  2006Kr07: E=140 MeV {+34}S beam was produced from the 15-UD Pelletron  
 36S 2c  accelerator at the Nuclear Science Centre, New Delhi, India. The target
 36S 3c  was 1.29-mg/cm{+2} enriched {+115}In. The deexciting |g rays were      
 36S 4c  detected using the Indian National Gamma Array (INGA), consisting of   
 36S 5c  eight Compton-suppressed HPGe Clover detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,     
 36S 6c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO), and |g|g(|q)(POL). Deduced levels, J, |p, and
 36S 7c  |g-ray multipolarities. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.     
 36S  cG E,RI$From 2006Kr07. |DE|g=1 keV is assumed by evaluators based on      
 36S 2cG typical uncertainties for the INGA array.                              
 36S  cG M$From measured |g|g(|q)(DCO) and |g|g(|q)(POL). Expected R{-DCO}      
 36S 2cG values in a stretched quadrupole gate are R{-DCO}(Q)|?1.05 for         
 36S 3cG stretched quadrupole (|DJ=2) or unstretched dipole (|DJ=0) transitions;
 36S 4cG R{-DCO}(Q)|?0.55 for stretched dipole (|DJ=1) transitions. Expected    
 36S 5cG R{-DCO} values in a stretched dipole gate are R{-DCO}(D)|?1.1 for      
 36S 6cG stretched dipole (|DJ=1) transitions; R{-DCO}(D)|?1.8 for stretched    
 36S 7cG quadrupole (|DJ=2) or unstretched dipole (|DJ=0) transitions. A        
 36S 8cG positive POL indicates an electric type transition, and a negative POL 
 36S 9cG indicates a magnetic type transition.                                  
 36S  cL E$From a least-squares fit to the measured |g-ray energies in 2006Kr07,
 36S 2cL unless otherwise noted.                                                
 36S  cL J$As given in 2006Kr07, unless otherwise noted. When considered in the 
 36S 2cL Adopted Levels, the firm assignments here are placed within parentheses
 36S 3cL if there are no other strong arguments to support these firm           
 36S 4cL assignments.                                                           
